          "section_id": "4edf1745",
          "title": "DeepONet (Deep Operator Network)",
          "text": "DeepONet was the first architecture to theoretically prove that neural networks can approximate any continuous nonlinear operator. It consists of two components:\n\u2022 Branch Network : Encodes the input function (e.g., initial or boundary conditions).\n\u2022 Trunk Network : Encodes the spatial coordinates where the output is evaluated.\nBy combining these representations, DeepONet can approximate solutions to differential equa- tions across different domains.",
